:50b980c579aae4a82aa9624e93348fad8c534b70d23acfee3b9fd0d4c4b70024", "source_text": "Set <MATH_0001>. The morphism <MATH_0002>\nfactors through the diagonal <MATH_0003> as it factors\nthrough <MATH_0004>. Hence <MATH_0005> because\n<MATH_0006>\nfor the fourth equality use\nCategories, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nLet <MATH_0007> be the projections.\nThe composition law <MATH_0008> constructed on <MATH_0009> in\nAlgebraic Stacks, Lemma <REF_0002>\nagrees with the group law on <MATH_0010> (proof omitted). Thus\nAlgebraic Stacks, Lemma <REF_0003>\nshows we obtain a canonical fully faithful <MATH_0011>-morphism\n<MATH_0012>\nof stacks in groupoids over <MATH_0013>. To see that it is\nan equivalence it suffices to show that it is essentially surjective.\nTo do this it suffices to show that any object of <MATH_0014> over\na scheme <MATH_0015> comes fppf locally from <MATH_0016> via a morphism <MATH_0017>, see\nStacks, Lemma <REF_0004>.\nHowever, this follows the condition that <MATH_0018> turns <MATH_0019>\ninto a gerbe over <MATH_0020>, see property (2)(a) of\nStacks, Lemma <REF_0005>.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nBy\nCriteria for Representability, Lemma <REF_0006>\nwe conclude that <MATH_0021> is flat and locally of finite presentation.\nFinally, <MATH_0022> is surjective, flat, and locally of finite\npresentation by\nCriteria for Representability, Lemma\n<REF_0007>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f43d376d27a9dbbf467e4a96ca16d6595389b5ce893da68cada9d608f3368176", "unit_id": "tag:06QG:proof"}
